Collections allows us to store multiple objects in a single unit.
or, Collections is used to store multiple objects.

Collections is an Interface, which extends Iterable interface, It is extended by few more interfaces, such as;
1. List
2. Set
3. Queue

Each of the interfaces is implemented by few classes
List, is implemented by: ArrayList, LinkedList, Stack and (Vector (vectors are not used much)).
Set, is implemented by: HashSet, LinkedHashSet, TreeSet and (EnumSet (Not used much)).
Queue, is implemented by: ArrayDequeue, PriorityQueue and LinkedList.

Map is a separate interface;
It is implemented by,
HashMap,
TreeMap,
LinkedHashMap,


Iterator is Implemented by ListIterator(not used).